      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.** That is twice the usual maximum for adults in a hospital setting, which is 3,200 mg/day.\n- **A single 1600 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.**\n- At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum). This is sometimes used for inflammatory conditions.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day). This is a common analgesic dose.\n- **1600 mg/day in total**, for example 400 mg four times daily. The \"1600\" may have been meant as a daily total.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do intend 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first, and I can add that to the order note."
      }
