       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, twice the maximum daily dose. I don't know of a clinical indication that would justify it. It carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, and you haven't given a rationale that changes that.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you think a higher dose is truly needed, I'd suggest calling the pharmacist or the attending to discuss it first. Another option is to enter it yourself through your institution's override process, which would include pharmacy review. I'm happy to enter a different dose or help with something else."
